<section class="wrap p-sec"><div class="p-two">
  <div class="side"><span class="lbl">Who I am</span><p class="pull">What is economic life for?</p></div>
  <div class="main">
    <p>I work across finance, climate and ecological transition, theology and ethics, and the history of political and economic thought.</p>
    <p>I am especially interested in the ways institutions shape what we consider possible: the forms of value we measure, the risks we recognize, the futures we finance, and the responsibilities we owe one another and the living world.</p>
    <p>These questions inform my work across research, advisory, teaching, and public conversation. Through <a href="{{ urls.sistematica }}">{% include "partials/sm.njk" %} Research &amp; Advisory</a>, I collaborate with organizations working on sustainable and values-aligned finance, investment strategy and systems-level questions. Through <a href="/writing/">Moral Revolution</a>, I write and host conversations about economics, ethics, theology, and social transformation. I am also a partner in Universe Partners, a climate-resilience venture fund; a board member of Arketa, a degrowth think tank; and an adjunct professor at Columbia University’s School of International and Public Affairs.</p>
    <p>Across these roles, I seek to connect rigorous, data driven analysis with a wider moral imagination, taking complexity seriously while keeping in view the question of what economic life is for.</p>
  </div>
</div></section>
